values ('f6b7c8d9-0e1f-4a76-9b56-6c7d8e9f0a16', 'introduction-to-psychology', 'Introduction to Psychology', 'This course introduces psychology as the scientific study of behavior, mind, brain, and social life. Students examine the field''s history, methods, biological foundations, sensation and perception, consciousness, learning, memory, cognition, development, motivation, emotion, personality, social behavior, psychological disorders, therapy, health, and applied psychology. The course emphasizes evidence, ethics, diversity, cultural context, and the practical value of psychological science.');

